<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<phpunit xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="vendor/phpunit/phpunit/phpunit.xsd"
         bootstrap="vendor/autoload.php"
         colors="true"
         failOnWarning="true"
         failOnRisky="true">
    <!-- The same JIT the CLI turns on in bin/console. The suite spends most of its time in the solver, and the
         tests do not go through bin/console, so it has to be said twice.

         **ON ITS OWN THIS ENTRY DOES NOTHING, AND ON 2026-09-11 IT WAS DOING NOTHING.** `opcache.jit` is
         settable at runtime but `opcache.jit_buffer_size` is `PHP_INI_SYSTEM` and defaults to 0, so with no
         buffer this selects a mode for a compiler with nowhere to emit code. Measured in the project
         container: buffer 0, `opcache_get_status()['jit']['enabled'] === false`. Whether a buffer was there
         in an earlier image is not knowable from here.

         **And with the buffer set, this suite is not one second faster for it**: 22:06.248 against 22:06.927.
         The JIT is worth 1.57x on the solver commands and nothing measurable here, which is TOOL-22. This entry
         stays because it costs nothing and because `SDWA5_FULL_REPLAY=1` turns this suite into something much
         more command shaped. The buffer is now set at startup in
         `.ddev/php/opcache-jit.ini` and in `ini-values` on setup-php in `.github/workflows/tests.yml`, and
         that is what actually turned the JIT on. Worth 1.61x on the compile hot path, measured at
         0.2327 s/scene interpreted against 0.1449 s/scene traced over an evenly spread 40-scene sample.

         Kept rather than deleted for the same reason as the call in `bin/console`: it is still what turns the
         JIT on where a buffer exists but no mode is set. -->
    <php>
        <ini name="opcache.jit" value="tracing"/>
    </php>
    <testsuites>
        <testsuite name="unit">
            <directory>tests</directory>
        </testsuite>
    </testsuites>
    <source>
        <include>
            <directory>src</directory>
        </include>
    </source>
</phpunit>
